Question: Simplify the Compilation Process

Link:
https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/9kh4giios2j4?lecture_hash=t5qc0u6ap8tg

Solution:
touch build.sh
echo '#!/bin/bash' > build.sh
echo 'gcc hello.c -o hello' >> build.sh
chmod 700 build.sh
./build.sh
./hello

Approach:
1. Touch command to create the build.sh file.
2. i'll use echo to add the shebang to the file.
3. echo again to add the gcc command to compile hello.c
4. Next, I used chmod 700 to give the owner read and write and execute
5. thenn I ran ./build.sh to compile the program and ./hello to see output.